# AGENTS.md

## Purpose

This repository is a Robot Framework robot package served as Operaton external
tasks by purjo. `pur serve .` polls the engine for configured topics, executes
the mapped Robot task, and returns process variables.

Use the terms **Operaton**, **robot package**, and **external task**. Follow
the `purjo-operaton-task-package` skill.

## Repository map

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `pyproject.toml` | Dependencies, purjo topics, and Vault profiles |
| `{{package}}_{{topic_words}}.robot` | `{{Task Name}}` task |
| `{{Package}}Client.py` | API client library |
| `{{Package}}Models.py` | Domain types, keyword input models, and API row models |
| `OperatonTasks.py` | Task contracts and (by default) element-template specs |
| `operaton-contracts` | PyPI package providing `TaskContract`, `Validate Task Input`, and template tooling |
| `OperatonTemplates.py` | Optional separate build-time template specs |
| `{{package}}-logo.svg` | Root-level build-time template icon |
| `.operaton/element-templates/` | Generated templates; never hand-edited |
| `examples/` | Example BPMN processes with start forms |
| `tests/` | pytest, RobotLibrary suites, HTTP stubs, manual variables |
| `Makefile` | Test, package, and serve commands |
| `uv.lock` | Resolved dependency graph; generated, never hand-edited |
| `.wrapignore` | Files excluded from `pur wrap` |

## Topic-to-task contract

| Topic | Robot task | Inputs | Outputs |
|---|---|---|---|
| `{{topic}}` | `{{Task Name}}` | `{{inputAlias}}` | `{{outputAlias}}` |

### Reserved topics

List topic names owned by other workers here and in
`[tool.operaton-contracts] reserved-topics`; `operaton-contracts check`
rejects them.

## Secrets

The `default` Vault profile reads `{{vault/path}}/demo-api`; `prod` reads
`{{vault/path}}/production-api`. Secrets are Robot `Secret` variables, never
logged or returned. `VAULT_ADDR` and `VAULT_TOKEN` must be set when serving.
The endpoint comes from `{{PACKAGE}}_API_ENDPOINT`.

## Development

```console
{{run}} make format
{{run}} make check
{{run}} make element-templates
{{run}} make test
{{run}} make check-element-templates
{{run}} make dist
{{run}} make serve
```

`make test` is offline; `make check-element-templates` fetches the pinned
schema from gitlab.com. Manage runtime dependencies with `uv add`, and
development tools in `devenv.nix` (devenv) or uv's `dev` group (uv). In
devenv mode, keep only `robotframework-robotlibrary` in the uv `dev` group;
devenv supplies pytest, pytest-cov, mypy, Black, and jsonschema.
